<Base title="Directory methodology" description="Baseline sources, unknown provider terms, editorial verification and calculator assumptions.">
<h1>Methodology and verification</h1>
<h2>Baseline candidates are not verified partners.</h2>
<p>The initial dataset lists five national qualified intermediary candidates and three cost segregation candidates. Null fields mean unknown; an explicit false means a negative assertion. Coverage, names and ownership groups are baseline editorial leads requiring current confirmation.</p>
<p>Provider fees, escrow terms, bonding, audit-defense terms and credentials are not inferred. Tier is unassigned until a commercial agreement exists. Sponsorship must be disclosed separately and cannot change state rules.</p>
<h2>Weekly validation is not weekly fact checking.</h2>
<p>The pipeline validates reviewed raw records and produces normalized records. It does not scrape websites, rewrite review dates or claim facts were freshly verified. A factual update requires an editorial source change and a new review date.</p>
<h2>State summaries have a narrow scope.</h2>
<p>Displayed rates describe individual state income tax only. California is variable. Corporate taxes, federal taxes, residency, state conformity and exchange eligibility need separate review.</p>
<h2>Structured data follows visible content.</h2>
<p>State pages include State, FinancialService and FAQPage nodes. FAQ answers match the visible answers. Structured data does not guarantee search placement, rich results or AI citations.</p>
<h2>Calculator limits</h2>
<p>The tool uses assumed allocations and CPA-confirmed excess depreciable basis. It excludes carryover basis and does not determine whether bonus depreciation is legally available. Short-life allocation is an assumption rather than a study result.</p>
</Base>
